==English==
[[File:Acetate-anion-3D-balls.png|thumb]]

===Etymology===
Formed from the root of {{bor|en|la|acētum||vinegar}} ({{suffix|en||ate}}), from {{m|la|aceō||I am sour}}; {{l|en|surface analysis#Noun}}, {{confix|en|acet|ate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæsɪteɪ̯t/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-acetate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q212527}} {{lb|en|organic chemistry}} Any [[ester]] or [[salt#Noun|salt]] of [[acetic acid]].
#: {{synonyms|en|ethanoate}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1819|author=Abraham Rees|title=The Cyclopædia
|passage={{...}} to pad a piece in diluted '''acetate''' of alumine to obtain a pale lemon ground {{...}}}}
# [[cellulose acetate|Cellulose acetate]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Workers World|author=Leslie Feinberg|url=https://ia804705.us.archive.org/23/items/lavender-and-red/Lavender_and_Red.pdf#page=361|title=How La Güinera made room for more gender|date=16 July 07|text=Performers use '''acetate''' because eyelash glue is not available. They create eyelashes out of horse hair or cut from carbon paper. Their nails are glued on with a shoe adhesive.}}
# A [[transparent#Adjective|transparent]] [[sheet#Noun|sheet]] used for [[overlay#Noun|overlays]].
# ''In full'' '''acetate disc''': a [[disc]] of [[aluminium]] [[cover#Verb|covered]] in a [[wax#Noun|wax]] [[use#Verb|used]] to [[make#Verb|make]] [[demonstration]] [[copy#Noun|copies]] of a [[phonograph]] [[record#Noun|record]].
#: {{cot|en|dubplate}}
#* '''2002''', Dave Thompson, ''The Music Lover's Guide to Record Collecting'', Hal Leonard Corporation ({{ISBN|9781617744921}}), [https://books.google.de/books?id=GtGGDwAAQBAJ&lpg=PT89&dq=record%20%22acetates%22&pg=PT89#v=onepage&q=record%20%22acetates%22&f=false Acetates—The Rock Star's Rough Draft]:
#*: '''Acetates''' are a relic of the days before cassettes, DAT, and recordable CDs came into widespread use in recording studios. Manufactured from aluminum, and coated in a thin sheet of vinyl, they were produced to allow the concerned parties to hear how a particular version of a recording would sound outside the studio, on their home hi-fi, for example.

